{"1-3":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":3,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"saul-h7586g","name":"Saul","kind":"person","brief":"King of Israel,","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"samuel-h8050g","name":"Samuel","kind":"person","brief":"Prophet and Judge","count":1,"firstVerse":3}],"places":[{"id":"hebron-h2275a","name":"Hebron","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":1}],"words":[{"base":"H2275","lemma":"חֶבְרוֹן","tr":"chev·ron","gloss":"Hebron","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":71},{"base":"H1571","lemma":"גַּם","tr":"gam","gloss":"also","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":769},{"base":"H1732","lemma":"דָּוִד","tr":"da·vid","gloss":"David","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1075},{"base":"H0859","lemma":"אַתָּ֫ה","tr":"at·tah","gloss":"you(m.s.)","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1092},{"base":"H8543","lemma":"תְּמוֹל","tr":"te·mol","gloss":"yesterday","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":23},{"base":"H8032","lemma":"שִׁלְשֹׁם","tr":"shil·shom","gloss":"three days ago","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":24},{"base":"H5057","lemma":"נָגִיד","tr":"na·gid","gloss":"leader","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":44},{"base":"H4886","lemma":"מָשַׁח","tr":"ma·shach","gloss":"to anoint","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":69},{"base":"H0587","lemma":"אֲנַ֫חְנוּ","tr":"a·nach·nu","gloss":"we","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":120},{"base":"H6106","lemma":"עֶ֫צֶם","tr":"e·tsem","gloss":"bone","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":126}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1SA","chapter":16,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now the LORD said to Samuel, “How long are you going to mourn for Saul, since I have rejected him as king over Israel? Fill your horn with oil and go. I am sending you to Jesse of Bethlehem, for I have selected from his sons a king for Myself.”","from":3},{"book":"1SA","chapter":16,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"So Jesse sent for his youngest son and brought him in. He was ruddy, with beautiful eyes and a handsome appearance. And the LORD said, “Rise and anoint him, for he is the one.”","from":3},{"book":"1SA","chapter":16,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"So Samuel took the horn of oil and anointed him in the presence of his brothers, and the Spirit of the LORD rushed upon David from that day forward. Then Samuel set out and went to Ramah.","from":3},{"book":"2SA","chapter":5,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Even in times past, while Saul was king over us, you were the one who led Israel out and brought them back. And to you the LORD said, ‘You will shepherd My people Israel, and you will be ruler over them.’”","from":2},{"book":"GEN","chapter":29,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Laban declared, “You are indeed my own flesh and blood.” After Jacob had stayed with him a month,","from":1},{"book":"NUM","chapter":13,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"They went up through the Negev and came to Hebron, where Ahiman, Sheshai, and Talmai, the descendants of Anak, dwelled. It had been built seven years before Zoan in Egypt.","from":1},{"book":"NUM","chapter":27,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"who will go out and come in before them, and who will lead them out and bring them in, so that the congregation of the LORD will not be like sheep without a shepherd.”","from":2},{"book":"DEU","chapter":17,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"you are to appoint over yourselves the king whom the LORD your God shall choose. Appoint a king from among your brothers; you are not to set over yourselves a foreigner who is not one of your brothers.","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2},{"id":"judges-era","title":"Judges era and the road to David","people":2}]},"4-9":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":5,"firstVerse":4},{"id":"jebusites-h2983g","name":"Jebusites","kind":"person","brief":"Canaanite tribe","count":2,"firstVerse":4},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":4},{"id":"joab-h3097g","name":"Joab","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":2,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"zeruiah-h6870g","name":"Zeruiah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of David","count":1,"firstVerse":6}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":4},{"id":"millo-h4407","name":"Millo","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8}],"words":[{"base":"H1732","lemma":"דָּוִד","tr":"da·vid","gloss":"David","lang":"h","inPassage":8,"uses":1075},{"base":"H2982","lemma":"יְבוּס","tr":"ye·vus","gloss":"Jebus","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H5892","lemma":"עִיר","tr":"ir","gloss":"excitement","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":1090},{"base":"H2983","lemma":"יְבוּסִי","tr":"ye·vu·si","gloss":"Jebusite","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":41},{"base":"H3427","lemma":"יָשַׁב","tr":"ya·shav","gloss":"to dwell","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1079},{"base":"H3097","lemma":"יוֹאָב","tr":"yo·av","gloss":"Joab","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":145},{"base":"H7223","lemma":"רִאשׁוֹן","tr":"ri·shon","gloss":"first","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":181},{"base":"H5439","lemma":"סָבִיב","tr":"sa·viv","gloss":"around","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":335},{"base":"H7218","lemma":"רֹאשׁ","tr":"rosh","gloss":"head","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":599},{"base":"H4407","lemma":"מִלּוֹא","tr":"mil·lo","gloss":"Millo","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2SA","chapter":3,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Now the war between the house of Saul and the house of David was protracted. And David grew stronger and stronger, while the house of Saul grew weaker and weaker.","from":9},{"book":"JDG","chapter":1,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The Benjamites, however, failed to drive out the Jebusites living in Jerusalem. So to this day the Jebusites live there among the Benjamites.","from":4},{"book":"2SA","chapter":8,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Joab son of Zeruiah was over the army; Jehoshaphat son of Ahilud was the recorder;","from":6},{"book":"ISA","chapter":41,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Do not fear, for I am with you; do not be afraid, for I am your God. I will strengthen you; I will surely help you; I will uphold you with My righteous right hand.","from":9},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"the Jebusites, the Amorites, the Girgashites,","from":4},{"book":"GEN","chapter":15,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Amorites, Canaanites, Girgashites, and Jebusites.”","from":4},{"book":"EXO","chapter":3,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And I have promised to bring you up out of your affliction in Egypt, into the land of the Canaanites, Hittites, Amorites, Perizzites, Hivites, and Jebusites—a land flowing with milk and honey.’","from":4},{"book":"JOS","chapter":15,"verse":16,"verseEnd":17,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Caleb said, “To the man who strikes down Kiriath-sepher and captures it, I will give my daughter Acsah in marriage.” So Othniel son of Calebʼs brother Kenaz captured the city, and Caleb gave his daughter Acsah to him in marriage.","from":6}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2}]},"10-14":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":3,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"hachmonites-h2453g","name":"Hachmonites","kind":"person","brief":"Family of warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"jashobeam-h3434g","name":"Jashobeam","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"ahoah-h0265","name":"Ahoah","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"dodo-h1734h","name":"Dodo","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"eleazar-h0499i","name":"Eleazar","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":12}],"places":[{"id":"philistia-h6429","name":"Philistia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"ephes-dammim-h0658","name":"Ephes-dammim","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13}],"words":[{"base":"H6450","lemma":"פַּס דַּמִּים","tr":"pas dam·mim","gloss":"Pas-dammim","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H1368","lemma":"גִּבּוֹר","tr":"gib·bor","gloss":"mighty man","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":159},{"base":"H6430","lemma":"פְּלִשְׁתִּי","tr":"pe·lish·ti","gloss":"Philistine","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":288},{"base":"H2513","lemma":"חֶלְקָה","tr":"chel·qah","gloss":"portion","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":29},{"base":"H5973","lemma":"עִם","tr":"im","gloss":"with","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1051},{"base":"H1732","lemma":"דָּוִד","tr":"da·vid","gloss":"David","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1075},{"base":"H2453","lemma":"חַכְמוֹנִי","tr":"chakh·mo·ni","gloss":"Hachmonite","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H3434","lemma":"יָשׇׁבְעָם","tr":"ya·shov·am","gloss":"Jashobeam","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H7969","lemma":"שָׁלֹשׁ","tr":"sha·losh","gloss":"three","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":431},{"base":"H0266","lemma":"אֲחוֹחִי","tr":"a·cho·chi","gloss":"Ahohite","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1SA","chapter":14,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So the LORD saved Israel that day, and the battle moved on beyond Beth-aven.","from":14},{"book":"1SA","chapter":16,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now the LORD said to Samuel, “How long are you going to mourn for Saul, since I have rejected him as king over Israel? Fill your horn with oil and go. I am sending you to Jesse of Bethlehem, for I have selected from his sons a king for Myself.”","from":10},{"book":"1SA","chapter":16,"verse":12,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So Jesse sent for his youngest son and brought him in. He was ruddy, with beautiful eyes and a handsome appearance. And the LORD said, “Rise and anoint him, for he is the one.” So Samuel took the horn of oil and anointed him in the presence of his brothers, and the Spirit of the LORD rushed upon David from that day forward. Then Samuel set out and went to Ramah. Now the Spirit of the LORD had departed from Saul, and a spirit of distress from the LORD began to torment him.","from":10},{"book":"1SA","chapter":17,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now the Philistines gathered their forces for war at Socoh in Judah, and they camped between Socoh and Azekah in Ephes-dammim.","from":13},{"book":"1SA","chapter":19,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"He took his life in his hands when he struck down the Philistine, and the LORD worked a great salvation for all Israel. You saw it and rejoiced, so why would you sin against innocent blood by killing David for no reason?”","from":14},{"book":"2SA","chapter":3,"verse":17,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now Abner conferred with the elders of Israel and said, “In the past you sought David as your king. Now take action, because the LORD has said to David, ‘Through My servant David I will save My people Israel from the hands of the Philistines and of all their enemies.’”","from":10},{"book":"2SA","chapter":3,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Abner said to David, “Let me go at once, and I will gather all Israel to my lord the king, that they may make a covenant with you, and that you may rule over all that your heart desires.” So David dismissed Abner, and he went in peace.","from":10},{"book":"2SA","chapter":23,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"These are the names of Davidʼs mighty men: Josheb-basshebeth the Tahchemonite was chief of the Three. He wielded his spear against eight hundred men, whom he killed at one time.","from":10}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"15-19":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":4,"firstVerse":15}],"places":[{"id":"philistia-h6429","name":"Philistia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"adullam-h5725","name":"Adullam","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"rephaim-valley-h7497g","name":"Rephaim Valley","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"bethlehem-h1035g","name":"Bethlehem","kind":"place","brief":"In Judah","count":3,"firstVerse":16}],"words":[{"base":"H1035","lemma":"בֵּית לֶ֫חֶם","tr":"bet le·chem","gloss":"Bethlehem","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":82},{"base":"H1732","lemma":"דָּוִד","tr":"da·vid","gloss":"David","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":1075},{"base":"H8354","lemma":"שָׁתָה","tr":"sha·tah","gloss":"to drink","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":217},{"base":"H6430","lemma":"פְּלִשְׁתִּי","tr":"pe·lish·ti","gloss":"Philistine","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":288},{"base":"H7969","lemma":"שָׁלֹשׁ","tr":"sha·losh","gloss":"three","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":431},{"base":"H0014","lemma":"אָבָה","tr":"a·vah","gloss":"be willing","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":54},{"base":"H0953","lemma":"בּוֹר","tr":"bor","gloss":"pit","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":66},{"base":"H0227","lemma":"אָז","tr":"az","gloss":"then","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":141},{"base":"H4264","lemma":"מַחֲנֶה","tr":"ma·cha·neh","gloss":"camp","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":215},{"base":"H8179","lemma":"שַׁ֫עַר","tr":"sha·ar","gloss":"gate","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":374}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"LEV","chapter":17,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"If anyone from the house of Israel or a foreigner living among them eats any blood, I will set My face against that person and cut him off from among his people.","from":19},{"book":"NUM","chapter":11,"verse":4,"verseEnd":5,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Meanwhile, the rabble among them had a strong craving for other food, and again the Israelites wept and said, “Who will feed us meat? We remember the fish we ate freely in Egypt, along with the cucumbers, melons, leeks, onions, and garlic.","from":17},{"book":"JOS","chapter":12,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"the king of Libnah, one; the king of Adullam, one;","from":15},{"book":"JOS","chapter":15,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"From there the border went up the Valley of Ben-hinnom along the southern slope of the Jebusites (that is, Jerusalem) and ascended to the top of the hill that faces the Valley of Hinnom on the west, at the northern end of the Valley of Rephaim.","from":15},{"book":"JDG","chapter":5,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Zebulun was a people who risked their lives; Naphtali, too, on the heights of the battlefield.","from":19},{"book":"JDG","chapter":9,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"for my father fought for you and risked his life to deliver you from the hand of Midian,","from":19},{"book":"1SA","chapter":7,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When they had gathered at Mizpah, they drew water and poured it out before the LORD. On that day they fasted, and there they confessed, “We have sinned against the LORD.” And Samuel judged the Israelites at Mizpah.","from":18},{"book":"1SA","chapter":10,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"After that you will come to Gibeah of God, where the Philistines have an outpost. As you approach the city, you will meet a group of prophets coming down from the high place, preceded by harps, tambourines, flutes, and lyres, and they will be prophesying.","from":16}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"20-25":{"people":[{"id":"abishai-h0052","name":"Abishai","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"joab-h3097g","name":"Joab","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"benaiah-h1141g","name":"Benaiah","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":2,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"jehoiada-h3077g","name":"Jehoiada","kind":"person","brief":"Father of warrior Benaiah","count":2,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"ariel-h0739","name":"Ariel","kind":"person","brief":"A Moabite","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":25}],"places":[{"id":"kabzeel-h6909","name":"Kabzeel","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"moab-h4124g","name":"Moab","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23}],"words":[{"base":"H7969","lemma":"שָׁלֹשׁ","tr":"sha·losh","gloss":"three","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":431},{"base":"H2595","lemma":"חֲנִית","tr":"cha·nit","gloss":"spear","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":47},{"base":"H4713","lemma":"מִצְרִי","tr":"mits·ri","gloss":"Egyptian","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":70},{"base":"H1141","lemma":"בְּנָיָ֫הוּ","tr":"be·na·yah","gloss":"Benaiah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":42},{"base":"H5221","lemma":"נָכָה","tr":"na·khah","gloss":"to smite","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":500},{"base":"H3077","lemma":"יְהוֹיָדָע","tr":"ye·ho·ya·da","gloss":"Jehoiada","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":51},{"base":"H3513","lemma":"כָּבֵד","tr":"ka·vad","gloss":"to honor: honour","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":113},{"base":"H4480","lemma":"מִן־","tr":"min","gloss":"from","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1187},{"base":"H0739","lemma":"אֲרִיאֵל","tr":"a·ri·el","gloss":"Ariel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H3381","lemma":"יָרַד","tr":"ya·rad","gloss":"to go down","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":380}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"DEU","chapter":3,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"(For only Og king of Bashan had remained of the remnant of the Rephaim. His bed of iron, nine cubits long and four cubits wide, is still in Rabbah of the Ammonites.)","from":23},{"book":"JOS","chapter":15,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"These were the southernmost cities of the tribe of Judah in the Negev toward the border of Edom: Kabzeel, Eder, Jagur,","from":22},{"book":"JDG","chapter":14,"verse":5,"verseEnd":6,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Samson went down to Timnah with his father and mother and came to the vineyards of Timnah. Suddenly a young lion came roaring at him, and the Spirit of the LORD came powerfully upon him, and he tore the lion apart with his bare hands as one would tear a young goat. But he did not tell his father or mother what he had done.","from":22},{"book":"1SA","chapter":17,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then a champion named Goliath, who was from Gath, came out from the Philistine camp. He was six cubits and a span in height,","from":23},{"book":"1SA","chapter":17,"verse":34,"verseEnd":36,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"David replied, “Your servant has been tending his fatherʼs sheep, and whenever a lion or a bear came and carried off a lamb from the flock, I went after it, struck it down, and delivered the lamb from its mouth. If it reared up against me, I would grab it by its fur, strike it down, and kill it. Your servant has killed lions and bears; this uncircumcised Philistine will be like one of them, for he has defied the armies of the living God.”","from":22},{"book":"1SA","chapter":17,"verse":51,"verseEnd":51,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"David ran and stood over him. He grabbed the Philistineʼs sword and pulled it from its sheath and killed him; and he cut off his head with the sword. When the Philistines saw that their hero was dead, they turned and ran.","from":23},{"book":"1SA","chapter":26,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And David asked Ahimelech the Hittite and Abishai son of Zeruiah, Joabʼs brother, “Who will go down with me to Saul in the camp?” “I will go with you,” answered Abishai.","from":20},{"book":"2SA","chapter":1,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Saul and Jonathan, beloved and delightful in life, were not divided in death. They were swifter than eagles; they were stronger than lions.","from":22}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":4}]},"26-47":{"people":[{"id":"joab-h3097g","name":"Joab","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":2,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"asahel-h6214g","name":"Asahel","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"dodo-h1734i","name":"Dodo","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"elhanan-h0445h","name":"Elhanan","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"pelonites-h6397","name":"Pelonites","kind":"person","brief":"Family of warrior","count":2,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"helez-h2503g","name":"Helez","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"shammah-h8048h","name":"Shammah","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"abiezer-h0044g","name":"Abiezer","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":28},{"id":"ikkesh-h6142","name":"Ikkesh","kind":"person","brief":"Father of warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":28},{"id":"ira-h5896h","name":"Ira","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":28},{"id":"ahoah-h0265","name":"Ahoah","kind":"person","brief":"David's war